{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793208071,"nonce":"4imQlLXCMWS7bEcMpoQdUDd+eCc=","message":"Broader verification of Pocket Studio BoardApp exposed a second path: deferred Signal.make calls inside imported files produce new SignalArray/SignalF64/etc. The entry-file retry alone leaves those imports failed. Import compilation now discovers and loads fresh modules from these unresolved-type suspensions, with a loaded-file guard set before nested graph discovery to prevent retry cycles. The portable fixture now puts the deferred macro call inside an imported Factory, whose generated Item inherits an unopened Base and calls another unopened module with an inferred return type. Ordinary constructors are excluded from this new check: applying it to all constructors regressed native stream virtual dispatch; limiting it to the lowering of deferred expansions restored StandardStreams, FileStreams and ProcessPipes. Final corpus and real-file rechecks are still pending.","files":null}]}